<div class="page">
  <h2 style="font-weight: bold;"><span data-field="section_heading_m">{{ section_heading_m }}</span></h2>
  <h3 style="font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px;"><span data-field="heading_campus">{{ heading_campus }}</span></h3>
  <p>
    <span data-field="paragraph_1">EIU Hosts Fall {{ year_2004 }} Commencement Ceremonies. Nearly {{ number_students_graduated }} students graduated from Eastern Illinois University during Fall {{ year_2004 }}, and more than half that number — about {{ number_students_participated }} — participated in formal commencement ceremonies Saturday, Dec. {{ month_dec }}, {{ year_2004 }}. (That number included some of the nearly {{ number_students_officially_graduated }} students who officially graduated at the end of the summer term in August.)</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="paragraph_2">Jean Wolski and Nancy Marlow, Eastern's faculty laureates for {{ year_2003 }} and {{ year_2004 }}, respectfully, co-presented the "Charge to the Class" during both the 10 a.m. and 2 p.m. ceremonies. Student Body President Christopher Getty of Lyons and Faculty Senate Chairperson David Carpenter also addressed the crowds.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="paragraph_3">{{ paragraph_3 }}</span>
  </p>
  <h4 style="margin-top: 20px; font-weight: bold;"><span data-field="heading_related_story">{{ heading_related_story }}</span></h4>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_1">{{ related_story_1 }}</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_2">{{ related_story_2 }}</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_3">Carpenter received his award during Eastern's 10 a.m. commencement ceremony Saturday, Dec. {{ month_dec }}, {{ year_2004 }}.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_4">Sixty-year-old Mendez, a former Eastern Illinois University professor of Spanish, died of a heart ailment in October {{ year_2003 }}. Less than two months later, friends and colleagues voted to establish an annual service award that would honor Mendez' memory. The award honors the person(s) who best exemplifies Mendez' dedication by his/her service to the university, profession and community at the local, national and/or international level. For the full story, see <a href="{{ url_story_1 }}">http://www.eiu.edu/pubaff/headlines/Carpenter.htm</a>.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_5">State Council Gives ${{ amount_state_council }} For EIU, Coles County Programs.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_6">The Illinois Arts Council recently awarded several grants to local organizations. A total of ${{ amount_state_council_2 }} in funding was presented to the Coles County Arts Council, EIU Celebration, the Tarble Arts Center (2) and the Karamu Association, which publishes a literary journal.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_7">{{ related_story_7 }}</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="related_story_8">The most recent installment of AGORA, the Department of English's online journal of ideas and creative expression, is now available at <a href="{{ url_story_2 }}">www.eiu.edu/agora</a>. Click to access the December issue, which features photographs of the overseas adventures of English faculty and students, together with poetry by David Radavich, essays by Angela Vietto and John Kilgore, and Julie Campbell's study of the Renaissance tradition of ranting debate over the role of women.</span>
  </p>
  <h4 style="margin-top: 20px; font-weight: bold;"><span data-field="heading_student_focus">{{ heading_student_focus }}</span></h4>
  <p>
    <span data-field="student_focus_1">{{ student_focus_1 }}</span>
  </p>
