  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="paragraph_5">Book attended the {{ year_attended }} 30th annual Student Laureate Award Ceremony at the Old State Capitol in Springfield, where she received a medallion and ${{ amount_medallion }}.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="paragraph_6">{{ paragraph_6 }}</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="paragraph_7">{{ paragraph_7 }}</span>
  </p>
  <h3 style="font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px;"><span data-field="heading_staff_faculty_news">{{ heading_staff_faculty_news }}</span></h3>
  <p>
    <span data-field="staff_news_1">{{ staff_news_1 }}</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="staff_news_2">Shirley A. Stewart, acting vice president for student affairs, announced her retirement, effective {{ date_retirement }}. "I've worked with Shirley for over 30 years," said EIU President Lou Hencken. "I am going to miss her and the work that she does in the student affairs area. She totally supports her staff and the students at EIU."</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="staff_news_3">Stewart, who received both her bachelor's and master's degrees in education from Eastern, served as a student assistant while Hencken was associate director of housing. Hencken recalled assigning her a particularly troublesome residence hall floor, even then having full faith in Stewart's ability to handle difficult situations. That was the start of her more than 30 years of experience in the field of higher education. For the full story, see <a href="{{ url_staff_news_1 }}">http://www.eiu.edu/pubaff/headlines/Stewart.htm</a>.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="staff_news_4">Marilyn Lisowski, early childhood, elementary, and middle level education, was awarded funding for her science, math, and technology program from the Illinois State Board of Education's Math and Science Partnership Program. Dr. Lisowski was funded for ${{ amount_lisowski }} to work with middle school and high school science and mathematics teachers in integrating technology into environmental science classes.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="staff_news_5">Doug Leahead, journalism/art, has been named to the board of directors of the James Jones Literary Society. In addition to preserving the memory and works of Jones, author of From Here to Eternity, The Thin Red Line, Whistle, Some Came Running, and others, the society in conjunction with Wilkes University annually awards a ${{ amount_leahead }} finest novelship fellowship in addition to creative writing awards.</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="staff_news_6">{{ staff_news_6 }}</span>
  </p>
